                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A geographic area owned or controlled by a single person or organization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2d89e16-d59d-47f4-a02a-cd763d22036e",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "The king ruled his domain harshly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8ab33fb-56c6-4612-a87f-d4558489edce",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "Bears and other ferocious beasts resented man's intrusion into their domain; so, too, did the Blackfoot Indians and other tribes, whose savage hostility was a constant menace to the lives of the toiling engineers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3390989c-c8ad-45cb-9482-bd8c2748f178",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "Farmers account for just 1.5% of the British population, but the size of their domain – 71% of the country’s surface area is classified as farmland – has given them power over the public imagination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b3b0f36-2c56-4955-9fb7-e216fcf3d3b7",
                                                "sense_id": "592130bc-dd54-3630-b5f3-56ef62ae482a",
                                                "text": "A blinded hermit in oblivion, disgraced\nLike Odysseus lost in Poseidon's endless domain\nIn a realm devoid ov solace, I roam"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A field or sphere of activity, influence or expertise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1001ed47-97a6-4bc8-aee8-1da3870787bb",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                                "text": "Dealing with complaints isn't really my domain: get in touch with customer services."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efc64990-921f-4801-bd67-004a39810610",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                                "text": "His domain is English history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "436c6d96-3ab1-43c1-a519-95eb8349da84",
                                                "sense_id": "f4fab948-dcce-3a44-9f03-abe880dc0758",
                                                "text": "When examining studies that assess independent living and social skills—key areas of focus in adulthood for individuals with ASD—it is observed that most research evaluates only one of these domains, either activities of daily living or social functioning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "156de277-f0c2-327b-a80f-a98b59da79c5",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of related items, topics, or subjects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce94ce98-d9ca-446b-8c86-66312b66e096",
                                                "sense_id": "156de277-f0c2-327b-a80f-a98b59da79c5",
                                                "text": "Some of the most beautiful and thus appealing physical theories, including quantum electrodynamics and quantum gravity, have been dogged for decades by infinities that erupt when theorists try to prod their calculations into new domains. Getting rid of these nagging infinities has probably occupied far more effort than was spent in originating the theories."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b67a4965-40ae-3ed4-84dd-3d5e4578dd33",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of input (argument) values for which a function is defined."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f0f0636-1cd9-37f5-9e6e-e202deba1de6",
                                        "entry_id": "af491e75-61b6-32f6-8c80-cfde93f369ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The set of input (argument) values for which a function is defined.",
                                            "The set A; The subset of A consisting of elements a of A such that there exists an element b in B with (a,b) in R."
